D={'schemaVersion':'1.0','title':'Telecom complaint investigation and controlled service credits','brief':brief,'assumptions':[],'stages':{s:{'items':[],'assumptions':[]} for s in ['context','tasks','components','workflow','framework','models','fmea','evals','rollout','export']}}
def h(i,s,w,o,v,b=True): D['assumptions'].append(dict(id=i,statement=s,why=w,owner=o,validation=v,launchBlocker=b))
h('H1','Proposed v1 serves authenticated consumer postpaid active connections in one tenant and currency; prepaid, enterprise, closed-service and cash-refund execution use an owned supervisor case.','Bound the ledger and eligibility semantics.','Product owner','Confirm supported segments, currency and meaning of active with operations.')
h('H2','Illustrative policy P1 allows outage credits only: verified outage overlap of at least 60 minutes; credit=floor(monthly base fee minor units * affected minutes / billing-cycle minutes), capped at the remaining eligible base fee and 1000 minor units per incident. Billing errors, poor speed without verified outage, larger amounts and uncertainty require supervisor review.','A concrete safe policy is needed to design the action boundary; these are not company rules.','Billing policy owner','Approve a versioned eligibility table, rounding, taxes, overlap rules, limits and customer consent requirements before writes.')
h('H3','Proposed APIs support tenant/customer/connection scoping, active-state versions, immutable policy versions, atomic incident credit uniqueness, durable operation lookup and fresh authorization at the billing writer.','The design cannot establish actual adapter capabilities.','Billing engineering lead','Prove these semantics in sandbox including unknown commit, conflicts and revoked permission. No autonomous credits if unavailable.')
h('H4','Proposed supervisor queue has a 48 elapsed-hour decision deadline from initial referral, acknowledgement within 15 minutes, updates at receipt and every 12 hours, escalation to duty lead at 36 hours and overdue transfer at 48 hours without approval by silence.','Brief supplies 48 hours but no staffing, clock or update cadence.','Customer operations lead','Confirm 24/7 staffing, elapsed UTC timer, escalation acceptance and notification channels.')
h('H5','Proposed privacy defaults keep full case evidence for 30 days and minimized financial audit references for 365 days, encrypted in tenant-resident storage; no raw payment details or entire bills in model prompts.','Retention and residency require company approval.','Privacy lead','Verify applicable retention, deletion, residency and model-provider terms before real data.')
h('H6','Illustrative planning assumptions are 10000 complaints/month, 80% reaching model investigation, 10% of those needing one schema retry; model budget prices are $2/input million and $8/output million tokens, not a vendor quote.','Reproducible capacity and budget without invented measured data.','AI platform owner','Measure shadow branch mix, token lengths and contracted prices.',False)
h('H7','Proposed credit API posts positive integer minor units as a CREDIT against a named original invoice line and incident; supervisor cannot override active-connection, subject, duplicate or freshness checks. A separate human process owns cash refunds and compensation.','Avoid introducing an unbounded general refund writer.','Finance operations lead','Confirm ledger allocation, credit semantics, supervisor authority and cash-refund handoff receipt.')
h('H8','Proposed authenticated case portal plus consented service notifications use template outbox messages; case status remains accessible if delivery fails.','Keep customers informed without inventing a live messaging integration.','Customer experience lead','Verify channel consent, accessible templates, delivery receipts and outbox deduplication.')
def add(st,i,k,t,de,re,da,hs=(),q=None):
 src=[{'type':'context','file':'user-brief','passage':q or 'Design a complaint assistant for a telecom provider.'}]
 src += [{'type':'hypothesis','file':x,'passage':next(a['statement'] for a in D['assumptions'] if a['id']==x)} for x in hs]
 z=dict(id=i,kind=k,title=t,description=de,reasoning=re,assumptions=list(hs),sources=src,data=da);D['stages'][st]['items'].append(z);return z

def ctx(i,t,v,hs=()):add('context',i,'context',t,v,'Choose a bounded release with explicit dependencies instead of inventing operational facts.',dict(field=t,value=v,question=''),hs)
ctx('CTX1','Decision and value','Resolve an authenticated customer complaint with an evidence-based explanation, a provable eligible credit, or a named supervisor disposition. Business decision: whether evidence and fresh policy authorize a specific service-credit posting. Hypothesis: reducing investigation effort improves seven-day durable resolution without increasing incorrect credits.',('H1','H2'))
ctx('CTX2','Actors and boundaries','Customer supplies issue/time/selected connection; account API authenticates ownership; model interprets minimized evidence; policy code computes; supervisor decides larger/unclear requests; billing writer commits; duty lead owns unresolved operations. Scope: outage, poor-speed and billing-error investigation; only verified eligible outage credit is automatic. Reject a general autonomous refund agent because cash movement and ambiguous causes need authority absent from the brief.',('H1','H7'))
ctx('CTX3','Start and completion','Start at authenticated complaint submission or resume by case ID; create a provisional case before evidence. Complete as credited only with ledger posting ID and operation readback; explained with evidence/no eligible auto-credit; cancelled before dispatch; duplicate linked to existing case/operation; or human-owned with queue receipt and due time. Pending/unknown are visible non-success states; never promise a refund while waiting.',('H3','H4'))
ctx('CTX4','Inputs and authoritative evidence','Session supplies tenant and customer, never request text. Active service registry supplies selected connection owner/status/version; billing supplies invoice line/base fee/cycle and credit ledger; network records supply outage incident and affected interval; policy registry supplies version; case store supplies history, revision and command key. Poor-speed evidence may be insufficient: no claim of a network cause without correlated records.',('H2','H3'))
ctx('CTX5','KPIs and capacity','R1 defines seven-day durable resolution and safety denominators; no baseline is known. Collect a two-week shadow baseline before experiment sizing. H6 capacity is illustrative; customer latency targets proposed: case acknowledgement 2 seconds, investigation p95 30 seconds excluding external wait, supervisor deadline 48 elapsed hours. No service restoration or network repair capability is designed.',('H4','H6'))
ctx('CTX6','Authority and launch dependency','All business actions are proposals. Default deployment is read-only until H1-H8 relevant approvals and adapter proofs exist. Human review cannot bypass deterministic identity, active service, atomic duplicate protection or version/approval binding. No provisioning, credential use, business writes or customer contact performed by this design.',('H3','H7','H8'))
ctx('CTX7','Data and customer experience','Minimize records to relevant invoice line, outage intervals and policy paragraphs; exclude card/bank data and unrelated connections. Customer sees case ID, source times, uncertainty, amount/currency if proved, queue owner and next update time. Cancellation stops undispatched credit; after an unknown or confirmed commit cancellation becomes an owned follow-up, never an automatic reversal.',('H5','H8'))

